            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:

- Receptacles

- Some windows (from the frame)

- Combustion air supply

During the infiltration test walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the items listed above. Airtightness is very important to achieve energy savings.

</airSeal>
                <VentilationSystem>The result of the infiltration test has shown that your house's natural air exchange is not enough. We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) and Energy Star certified, to ensure proper ventilation inside your home.</VentilationSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>You are thinking of installing a heat pump? This type of heating system can use up to 3 times less energy than a typical baseboard and needs electricity to operate. However, this kind of system can?????????t operate at a temperature below -250C, it then will require a secondary system to maintain the heat. In this case, the furnace can ensure the heat and the ducting system can be used by the heat pump to supply heat in the entire building. You might be eligible to participate in the Heat Pumps pilot project, please follow the link below for more information;

https://yukon.ca/en/news/expanded-rebates-renewable-home-heating-now-available



</HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
